{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>One crushed (פצוע דכה).</b> This is one whose testicles were split or one of them. <b>And severed (וכרות שפכה).</b> One whose organ was cut off — the vessel through which he pours out the water and the seed." "<b>In the assembly of HaShem.</b> That he not be counted as one of the assembly of HaShem to take a daughter of Israel. And the reason is that the essence of marriage is for procreation (Isaiah 45:18): ״כי לא תהו בראה לשבת יצרה״ — 'for not as emptiness did He create it; He formed it to be inhabited'; and since these are not fit to beget children, such marriages are for naught." "<b>And from the fact</b> that it says 'in the assembly of HaShem,' it appears that he is permitted to a woman who is not of the assembly of HaShem, such as a convert or a freedwoman, for Scripture did not say 'a crushed one and a severed one shall not marry a woman' — for if it had said so, it would be inferred from this that intercourse not for the perpetuation of the species was forbidden; but now, from the fact that it forbade him 'in the assembly of HaShem' and permitted him outside 'the assembly of HaShem,' it indicates that intercourse is permitted even not for the perpetuation of the species."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:31.420544443Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}